  "formatted_code_T004": "<div class='report'>\n  <h1>Countdown Timer Code Report</h1>\n\n  <div class='executive-summary'>\n    <h2>Executive Summary</h2>\n    <p>This report provides the complete HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code required to create a visually appealing countdown timer. The timer is designed with a dark theme and includes clear instructions for integrating the files. The CSS styles the timer with a modern, dark aesthetic, while the JavaScript handles the countdown logic. The HTML provides the structure. All code is optimized for readability and ease of use.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>HTML Code (index.html)</h2>\n  <p>The HTML file provides the basic structure for the countdown timer. It includes a container for the timer and placeholders for minutes and seconds.</p>\n  <pre><code class=\"language-html\">\n&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=\"en\"&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset=\"UTF-8\"&gt;\n    &lt;meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Countdown Timer&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;div class=\"timer-container\"&gt;\n        &lt;div id=\"timer-display\"&gt;\n            &lt;span id=\"minutes\"&gt;00&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;span id=\"seconds\"&gt;00&lt;/span&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n  </code></pre>\n\n  <h2>CSS Code (style.css)</h2>\n  <p>The CSS file styles the countdown timer with a dark theme, providing a visually appealing and user-friendly interface.</p>\n  <pre><code class=\"language-css\">\nbody {\n    background-color: #121212;\n    color: #ffffff;\n    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: center;\n    align-items: center;\n    min-height: 100vh;\n    margin: 0;\n}\n\n.timer-container {\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 20px;\n    border: 1px solid #333;\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);\n}\n\n.timer-display {\n    font-size: 2.5em;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n    color: #bb86fc;\n    text-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);\n}\n\n.timer-label {\n    font-size: 0.8em;\n    margin: 0 10px;\n    color: #a7a7a7;\n}\n\n#countdown {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 10px;\n}\n\n.time {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: center;\n}\n\n.time span {\n    font-size: 1.2em;\n    padding: 5px 10px;\n    background-color: #212121;\n    border-radius: 5px;\n}\n\n  </code></pre>\n\n  <h2>JavaScript Code (script.js)</h2>\n  <p>The JavaScript file contains the logic for the countdown timer, updating the display every second and handling the timer's completion.</p>\n  <pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">\n// script.js\n\n// Set the initial countdown time in minutes\nlet countdownMinutes = 5;\n\n// Calculate the total seconds\nlet time = countdownMinutes * 60;\n\n// Get the countdown display element from the HTML\nconst countdownDisplay = document.getElementById(\"countdown\");\n\n// Function to update the countdown display\nfunction updateCountdown() {\n  const minutes = Math.floor(time / 60);\n  let seconds = time % 60;\n\n  // Add a leading zero to seconds if it's less than 10\n  seconds = seconds &lt; 10 ? '0' + seconds : seconds;\n\n  // Update the HTML display with the current time\n  countdownDisplay.textContent = `${minutes}:${seconds}`;\n\n  // Decrement the time\n  time--;\n\n  // Check if the countdown has reached zero\n  if (time &lt; 0) {\n    clearInterval(countdownInterval);\n    countdownDisplay.textContent = \"TIME'S UP!\";\n    // You can add more actions here when the countdown finishes, like playing a sound or showing an alert.\n  }\n}\n\n// Update the countdown every second\nconst countdownInterval = setInterval(updateCountdown, 1000);\n\n// Initial call to set the display immediately\nupdateCountdown();\n  </code></pre>\n\n  <h2>Integration Instructions</h2>\n  <p>To integrate these files and create the countdown timer, follow these steps:</p>\n  <ol>\n    <li>Create three files: <code>index.html</code>, <code>style.css</code>, and <code>script.js</code>.</li>\n    <li>Copy the HTML code into <code>index.html</code>.</li>\n    <li>Copy the CSS code into <code>style.css</code>.</li>\n    <li>Copy the JavaScript code into <code>script.js</code>.</li>\n    <li>Link the CSS file to the HTML file by adding the following line within the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> tags:\n      <code>&lt;link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\"&gt;</code>\n    </li>\n   <li>Add the script to the body <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> tags:\n            <code>&lt;script src=\"script.js\"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code>\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n\n  <h2>Running the Files</h2>\n  <p>Ensure all three files (<code>index.html</code>, <code>style.css</code>, and <code>script.js</code>) are in the same directory. Open <code>index.html</code> in a web browser to view the countdown timer.</p>\n\n  <h2>Comprehensive Timer Layout Analysis</h2>\n    <h3>Layout HTML Analysis</h3>\n    <p>There are two layouts available (layout_html_1A and layout_html_2A) in the schema.  layout_html_1A uses span tags with IDs minutes and seconds, while layout_html_2A uses a simpler div structure.</p>\n    <pre><code class=\"language-html\">\n&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=\"en\"&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset=\"UTF-8\"&gt;\n    &lt;meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Countdown Timer&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;div class=\"timer-container\"&gt;\n        &lt;div id=\"timer-display\"&gt;\n            &lt;span id=\"minutes\"&gt;00&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;span id=\"seconds\"&gt;00&lt;/span&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n    </code></pre>\n\n    <pre><code class=\"language-html\">\n&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Timer&lt;/title&gt;\n    &lt;link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\"